n of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\n- $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$\n- $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n- $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,1]$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/assets/78af77d697ea292385e2bd2570c8185c728f57cc70c3edcc25ecccd0e84780e8.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangles II and III do not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangle I cover the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}]}
